# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The teacher response cache. Content-addressed provider payloads, including the
# ones the validator rejected, so it is both large and the least reviewed text in
# the tree. It is a resume aid, never an artifact: its hit rate is reported and
# the parquet is what gets published.
.cache/

# Secrets / local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Data artifacts are DVC-tracked, never Git-tracked. Cambridge-derived text is
# private (redistribution rights unverified).
data/*
!data/*.py
!data/gec/
!data/gec/*
*.sqlite
*.db


# The DVC cache holds the content of every tracked artifact, so committing it
# commits the data itself. W&I+LOCNESS is licensed for non-commercial research
# and permits publishing excerpts of under 100 words only, so its converted rows
# must not enter a Git remote. `.dvc/config` sets `no_scm`, which means DVC does
# not write its own ignore file and this has to be stated here.
.dvc/cache/
.dvc/tmp/

# Training / eval outputs
outputs/
checkpoints/
wandb/
# Generated eval reports at the repo root. Anchored with a leading slash: the
# bare pattern also matched `plans/reports/`, which is written research rather
# than generated output, and excluding it silently lost documented findings.
/reports/
# Adapter weights and run artifacts. Hundreds of MB of binaries that belong in
# DVC or W&B artifacts, not in Git history.
runs/

# Local tool state
.codegraph/
.claude/
.gemini/